Hello,

I got an AlphaServer 400 and it looks okay. I mean it is in mint
condition. No dust, original components, etc.
The problem that I have is that the unit doesn't power on. When I push
the power button nothing happens. I checked the 110V - 230V switch on
the back before I plugged the power cord and it was setup to 230V (EU
based).

I saw that it has two pair of cables coming from PSU, one for system
fan and one for a sensor which is mounted in from of the system fan.
Both cables look fine.

I removed the PSU and opened it and the is no dust, no burned
components as I can see. I measured the fuse on the top board and it
is okay and also measured the input-output from the top small board
and it is okay.

When I start the PSU with the cover removed I can hear the transformer
that is working.

Is there any trick to power the AlphaServer? It has some kind of
protection that doesn't allow me to power it on?
It would be nice to have a schematic so I can check further the
components. If someone has it please contact me on private or share it
here.

Thank you!


