The covers are all installed? On several alphaserver models the top
cover also operates a switch inside the system.
With the cover absent, you can't power on the system (unless you put
operate the switch with a screwdriver).
The same may apply to an AlphaServer 400. The installation guide
(still available on the HP site) doesn't have a clear drawing.

The power supply is connected to the main board, right?
- Did you check whether all components are seated properly in their
slots (ISA, EISA and PCI cards, memory cards etc).
- does the power led (top led) light up when the power is switched on?
- the power supply is switched to the correct mains voltage?

Read chapter 4 of the Installation Guide, it deals with
troubleshooting of the AlphaServer 400.
Hans


