A couple of things:
1) An AlphaServer 400 is (if I remember rightly) an AlphaStation 400
with a different software bundle, and maybe a different badge. So have
a look for AlphaStation 400 docs (or parts). E.g. there is an
AlphaStation 400 Technical Info doc at http://ftp.kaist.ac.kr/NetBSD/misc/d=
ec-docs/ek-pcdsa-ti.pdf.gz
(also covers the AlphaStation 200, similar electronics, different box,
different PSU).
2) The PSU was a buy-in and is probably regarded as an "if it's
broken, swap it" part so there'll be no specific PSU docs,
faultfinding, or (probably) schematic. The vendor name and model
should be on it. It isn't industry standard AT or ATX or similar...
3) Please don't assume that any given switched mode PSU (which this
surely will be?) will operate correctly without a realistic load. It
is entirely possible for SMPSUs to not start or otherwise misbehave if
they have no load.

Sorry I can't yet offer more than that.
Best of luck
John Wallace


