I just checked the "RSTS/E System Directives Manual" dated October 1985 
for RSTS/E V9.1 namely chapters 6 and 7 which deal with the RT11 Runtime 
System and RT11 Emulator Directives.  The first word of Core Common is 
the [PPN] value (or zero to use the current PPN) but there is no 
specific reference that this is used by the RT11 .CHAIN EMT request.
There is also a caveat that .CHAIN can only be used to pass control to 
another program under the RT11 runtime system.

A copy of this manual can be found online as a PDF document at 
http://elvira.stacken.kth.se/rstsdoc/rsts-doc-v92/

If you would like a copy of a more recent RSTS/E disk image to try using 
John Wilson's E11 or Bob Supnik's SIMH pdp11 emulator e-mail me using my 
firstname dot lastname at computer dot org.

Tony Nicholson


